# Dorn script patterns

Follow existing mods in this workspace. Typical `_main.script` layout:

```lua
local MOD_ID = "dorn_example"  -- matches .mod_id file
local DORN_COMMON_VERSION = "dorn_common_<hash>" -- managed by sync-dorn-common.sh, do not hand-edit

local DORN

function on_game_start()
	DORN = _G[DORN_COMMON_VERSION].load(MOD_ID)
	-- register callbacks, read MCM via on_option_change
end
```

## Naming and files

| Item | Pattern |
|------|---------|
| Main logic | `dorn_<feature>_main.script` or `zzz_dorn_<feature>_NN_<area>.script` for large mods |
| MCM registration | `dorn_<feature>_mcm.script` or `zzz_dorn_<feature>_mcm.script` |
| Entry hook | `zzzz_dorn_<feature>_main.script` when splitting across files |
| MOD_ID | snake_case, matches `.mod_id` and MCM namespace |
| MCM keys | `"main/foo"`, `"development/debug_log"` via `DORN.mcm.bool/number/string/key` |

## Boot and globals

- Never call `process_file()` from a script being auto-loaded.
- Resolve `DORN` inside `on_game_start()` only.
- Synced common files: `dorn_mcm_<hash>.script`, `dorn_dbg_<hash>.script`, `dorn_sys_<hash>.script`, `dorn_common_<hash>.script` - do not hand-edit hashes.
- Debug logging: `DORN.dbg.write(MOD_ID, slot.order, "[Tag] msg", slot.color)` behind `CONFIG.debug_log`.

## Style

- Tabs for indentation, LF line endings (see `.editorconfig`).
- `local function` for module-private helpers; `function on_game_start()` etc. for engine callbacks.
- CONFIG table for MCM-backed settings; LOG table for debug slot metadata.
- Prefer inline logic over one-off helpers. Comments only for non-obvious engine behavior.
